PATCH 156: the ACCEPT-cascade sim-reset + FSG-open base-losses (FUN_0000_4754 / 5f52 / 0291).

The mission-start cascade's setup step FUN_0000_4754 -> 4779 resets the sim state then FUN_0000_d501
parses <battle>.FSG.  Three asm-verified base-losses (vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin), each a SIGSEGV:
  * 4754: the d501 open passed the filename as the HOST pointer `&DAT_2000_39a9` (truncated into the
    16-bit INT-21h DX -> garbage) instead of the DOS offset 0x79a9.  The sibling FUN_0000_476a already
    passes a plain offset (0x79b9); mirror it (host-pointer-into-DOS-register class, patch 077/146).
  * 5f52 (asm): 8 near-offset entries at DGROUP:0x7d2a, each `di=word[DGROUP:0x7d2a+i*2]; byte[DGROUP:di]=0`
    -- Ghidra deref'd the near-offset di as a host pointer.  Rebase to g_mem+0x1c000.
  * 0291 (asm 0x291): the LFSR RNG.  SS=0x2ba9 (base 0x2ba90); a rolling word pointer ss:0x1f82 cycles
    0x1f84..0x1f8a, v=ss:[ptr], `shr v,1`; if the shifted-out bit was set, v^=0xb400; store back;
    ss:0x342(=DAT_2000_bdd2)=v-1; return v-1.  Ghidra deref'd ss:[bx] as a HOST pointer, used 32-bit
    width, and mislabelled the 0x1f84/0x1f8a bound immediates as DAT_1000_df84/df8a addresses.  Rebase
    to g_mem+0x2ba90, 16-bit.  (Load-bearing for deterministic RNG state per CLAUDE.md.)
Verified via the throwaway ACCEPT-cascade trace: with these + patch 155, the cascade runs crash-free
through e459 (LOADING.MS3/MRL) and the whole 4779 sim-reset (4413/5f52/9be8/b158/61f7/9d3c/b2a2/9cdb +
0291/9a32), stopping at the shared trig helper FUN_0000_05e2 (`*(uint*)(iVar6+0x2042)` DS-table base-loss)
-- the documented next frontier.  All three functions are reached ONLY by the ACCEPT mission cascade
(not yet wired into a verify flow) -> behaviour-neutral for the 19 covered flows.

